@startuml
!theme plain
title Digital Wallet — Issuer-Assisted Card Token Provisioning (Educational)
actor Cardholder
participant "Device Wallet" as Wallet
participant "Platform Provisioning Service" as Platform
participant "Network Tokenization Service" as Network
participant "Issuer Token Service" as Issuer
participant "Secure Device Credential Store" as Device
Cardholder -> Wallet : Add existing card
Wallet -> Platform : Check device and provisioning eligibility
Platform --> Wallet : Session context (illustrative)
Cardholder -> Wallet : Provide card details in protected UI
Wallet -> Platform : Submit protected enrollment request
Platform -> Network : Tokenization request
Network -> Issuer : Eligibility and risk verification
alt Issuer requires cardholder verification
  Issuer --> Network : Step-up required
  Network --> Platform : Verification choice
  alt Supported out-of-band code
    Cardholder -> Wallet : Enter issuer-provided code
    Wallet -> Platform : Submit verification response
    Platform -> Network : Verify cardholder
    Network -> Issuer : Verify evidence
  else Supported issuer-app verification
    Cardholder -> Issuer : Confirm in issuer app
    Issuer --> Network : Issuer confirmation
  end
else No step-up required
  Issuer --> Network : Eligibility confirmed
end
Network --> Platform : Authorized token provisioning result
Platform --> Wallet : Protected activation information
Wallet -> Device : Install/activate device credential
Device --> Wallet : Provisioning status
Wallet --> Cardholder : Show verified activation result
note bottom of Network
No scheme-specific cryptograms, payloads or keys are specified.
Actual Apple / Visa / issuer contracts govern this flow.
end note
@enduml